,p_plug_display_sequence=>10
,p_location=>null
,p_plug_source=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>',
'This page demonstrates how to manage JSON data in Oracle APEX using two different approaches. It includes an Interactive Report that can be switched via a region selector to display support ticket data either from the <strong>EBA_DEMO_JSON_SUPPORT_TI'
||'CKET</strong> JSON source (created on top of the underlying support ticket collection table) or as <strong>Raw JSON Documents</strong> showing the underlying JSON payloads directly. In both cases, the support ticket information is queried, displayed,'
||' and managed through Oracle APEX, enabling flexible exploration and maintenance of JSON-based data.',
'</p>',
'',
'<p>',
'To get started, use the region selector to switch between the <strong>Report View on Data Source</strong> and the <strong>Raw JSON Documents</strong>. In the report view, you can browse existing support tickets, create new entries, and perform search'
||', filter, sort, edit, or delete operations directly from the Interactive Report. The Raw JSON Documents view allows you to inspect the underlying JSON documents that store the support ticket data.',
'</p>',
'',
'<p>',
'Below the report, the <strong>Status Distribution</strong> and <strong>Priority Distribution</strong> pie charts provide a visual overview of support tickets by status and priority, helping users quickly analyze ticket trends and workload distributio'
||'n.',
'</p>'))
,p_attributes=>wwv_flow_t_plugin_attributes(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
